# oracle: native binary restart (serial file, b332f28 write_restart) of pair_style yukawa (pair_yukawa.cpp; settings kappa, cut_global, offset, mix; per pair a, cut); the 108-atom lj melt (50 steps) is written natively with that pair style, then read and continued for 100 steps
# oracle-inputs: w185nr_yukawa.restart
# native: b332f28 built as the parity binary wrote w185nr_yukawa.restart (atom_style atomic)
read_restart    w185nr_yukawa.restart
neighbor        0.3 bin
thermo_style    custom step temp epair emol etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
fix             1 all nve
run             100
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-12
# measured: max relative error 2.8e-15 (native restart continuation, engine vs native thermo and per-atom), so the tolerance is 1e-9
